\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Backgrounds and symmetry}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Which changes of labels preserve equations, Gaussian expectations
and a chosen marginal? Endpoint transport and coherent edge reversals
control the incidence map; the half-turn of the alternating cycle gives
a concrete action. Perfect pairings and a chosen retained split then
transport the operators and observable functionals. The
[duality](fdip-001F), [split-map](fdip-001T) and
[normalized-functional](fdip-0021) conventions are assumed.}

\p{A [finite background](fdip-000G) records the supplied data.
The [Gaussian integral](fdip-002T) and [marginal theorem](fdip-000E)
identify transported functionals with normalized laws. Fixed labels,
broken weights and nonstable partitions give different failures.
The [trace ratio](fdip-003H) distinguishes weighted cycles even under
a broader comparison allowing positive scaling. These examples prepare
[enriched-background comparisons](fdip-001E), where the permitted
arrows must specify exactly what survives.}

